-- HoodItemMeshes setup: paste ALL of this into Studio's Command Bar (View > Command Bar) and press Enter, right after
-- importing the four hood/art/models/items/Items_*.glb files with the 3D Importer (see hood/art/MESH_IMPORT.md).
-- (GENERATED by hood/tools/blender/build_item_package.py from studio_item_meshes.template.lua: edit the template.)
--
-- What it does, in one go (safe to run again after a re-import):
--   * finds the imported MeshParts (named <ItemId>, <ItemId>_2 ..., <ItemId>_Glow_<hex>) in the selection, or
--     anywhere in Workspace when nothing is selected;
--   * files them into ReplicatedStorage.HoodItemMeshes as one Model per item id, replacing an item already there;
--   * keeps each body mesh's palette texture, sets every _Glow_ part to Neon in its colour;
--   * anchors everything; big things (gate, boards, stands, portal, cliff, buildings ...) collide with a Box shape,
--     small props do not collide, guns are Massless with no collision;
--   * stores each item's design bounds (DesignMin / DesignMax), gun muzzles and collision class as attributes so the
--     game places them exactly, whatever unit the importer used;
--   * removes the empty imported models and prints what it made. Then: File > Save (or Publish).
